<title>USA: US Speaker Gingrich welcomes Clinton plan for D.C..</title>
<headline>US Speaker Gingrich welcomes Clinton plan for D.C..</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Republican House Speaker Newt Gingrich said Thursday he welcomed President Clinton's plan to help the U.S. capital city.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm delighted the president has put forth an initiative on the District of Columbia,&quot; Gingrich told reporters. &quot;I look foward to working with the administration to see if we can't make progress.&quot;</p>
<p>He said he had not had time to study the details of the $3.9 billion, five-year, aid package for the financially struggling capital. The White House announced the plan on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
